metacircular-univalent-unison-of-cubically-receptive-stateboxes-lines-7 : List (List Word)
metacircular-univalent-unison-of-cubically-receptive-stateboxes-lines-7 = cons "Reception is also a human fact. A mind that learns another's code of language at contact is receptive; a standard imposed on the channel narrows it. The exposition of language and inhibition names the opposite: inhibition is a selection refused, reception a selection made. A cubically receptive process takes the boundary another presents, in that other's terms, and fills it. That is what meeting a person's language means in construction." (cons "" nil)
